  "step_3": "The decision reason requires identifying outcomes with probability > 1/n (n = 2 → >0.5) and computing the average of such outcomes. In this case, only Lottery B has a probable outcome (2000 € at 100% > 50%), while Lottery A has no probable outcomes (both at 50% exactly). The reason would thus prefer B. However, the verbal report does not mention the threshold of 1/n or the concept of 'probable outcomes' at all. The individual's reasoning is based on emotional reactions (euphoria), risk aversion, certainty, and perceived value of a guaranteed gain, not on a formal calculation of probable outcomes. There is no reference to comparing outcomes by their probability relative to 1/n. Therefore, the individual did not use the specified decision reason. The reasoning process is qualitatively different and does not align with the rule of the decision reason.",
